lue","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that can be presented with a keyboard shortcut.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene’s keyboard shortcut is bound to the command it adds for creating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new windows (in the case of "},{"code":"WindowGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bringing a singleton window forward (in the case of "},{"code":"Window","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and, on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macOS, "},{"code":"Settings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Pressing the keyboard shortcut is equivalent to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selecting the menu command."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases where a command already has a keyboard shortcut, the scene’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keyboard shortcut is used instead. For example, ","type":"text"},{"code":"WindowGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" normally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"creates a File > New Window menu command whose keyboard shortcut is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"⌘N","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The following code changes it to ","type":"text"},{"code":"⌥⌘N","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".keyboardShortcut(\"n\", modifiers: [.option, .command])"]},{"text":"Localization","type":"heading","anchor":"Localization","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Provide a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localization"},{"type":"text","text":" value to specify how this shortcut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be localized."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Given that "},{"code":"key","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is always defined in relation to the US-English"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keyboard layout, it might be hard to reach on different international"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layouts. For example the shortcut "},{"code":"⌘[","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" works well for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"US layout but is hard to reach for German users, where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"[","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is available by pressing "},{"code":"⌥5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", making users type "},{"code":"⌥⌘5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The automatic keyboard shortcut remapping re-assigns the shortcut to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an appropriate replacement, "},{"code":"⌘Ö","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in this case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Providing the option","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/KeyboardShortcut\/Localization-swift.struct\/custom","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disables the automatic localization for this shortcut to tell the system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that internationalization is taken care of in a different way.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines a keyboard shortcut for opening new scene windows."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/keyboardshortcut(_:modifiers:locali